<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan's Engro rises 3.91 percent.</title>
<headline>Pakistan's Engro rises 3.91 percent.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-02-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Engro Chemical Pakistan Ltd's 10-rupee stock rose seven rupees, or 3.91 percent, to 186 on Tuesday on buying by overseas long-term investors following a 77 percent rise in its after-tax annual profits and higher payments of dividends and bonus issue, dealers said.</p>
<p>Some 7,000 Engro shares changed hands in early trade at the Karachi Stock Exchange, one dealer said.</p>
<p>Engro, Pakistan's second largest urea manufacturer with a market share of almost 24 percent, last week announced an 80 percent cash dividend and 25 percent bonus stocks for 1996, compared to 60 percent and 20 percent for 1995. Net profit rose to 1.386 billion rupees from 782 million.</p>
<p>-- Ibrahim Khan 9221-5685192</p>
